Package: agentos-core
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, python3-psutil, adduser
Recommends: agentos-runtime-dsh, agentos-desktop
Suggests: agentos-gnome-extension
Description: AgentOS core service
 The task manager, policy engine, audit trail, and read-only System Bridge of
 AgentOS, served over a Unix domain socket. The service runs as the unprivileged
 agentos system user and installs no privileged executor: every operation it can
 perform is declared in a capability manifest with an explicit privilege level,
 and the shipped policy permits read-only inspection only.
 .
 The package installs no network listener. Policy decisions, approvals, and
 execution results are recorded in an append-only audit trail.

Package: agentos-runtime-dsh
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, agentos-core (>= ${source:Version})
Recommends: nodejs (>= 22.19.0)
Description: DeepSeek Harness runtime adapter for AgentOS
 The AgentOS AgentRuntime adapter that drives a locked DeepSeek Harness
 revision through its SDK JSON-RPC stdio profile. The adapter spawns the
 harness with an allowlisted environment, maps its session events onto the
 AgentOS runtime event vocabulary, and reports unsupported capabilities
 honestly instead of simulating them.
 .
 Node.js is a Recommends rather than a Depends on purpose: no Node.js in
 Ubuntu 22.04 or 24.04 satisfies the locked harness requirement
 (^22.19.0 || >=24.0.0), so a hard dependency would make this package
 uninstallable on the target release. Install a qualifying Node.js from a
 source you trust and verify it with 'agentosctl doctor', which reports the
 exact requirement and the version it found. The adapter refuses to start on an
 unsupported Node.js and names the requirement, rather than silently running on
 an unverified environment.
 .
 This package does not download, build, or redistribute the harness.

Package: agentos-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, agentos-core (>= ${source:Version}),
 python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, python3-dbus, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1,
 dbus-user-session | dbus-x11
Description: AgentOS desktop application
 The GTK4 and libadwaita AgentOS window: conversation, task queue, system
 overview, the approval queue, the activity and audit view, and a read-only
 settings view. It also provides the per-login session broker that serves
 org.agentos.Session1 on the user session bus for the GNOME Shell extension.
 .
 Closing the window never stops a task: the core service owns task lifetime.
 The application holds no model credential, never runs as root, and never
 decides a policy question itself.

Package: agentos-gnome-extension
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, gnome-shell (>= 42), agentos-desktop (>= ${source:Version})
Description: AgentOS GNOME Shell extension
 The AgentOS panel entry for GNOME Shell 42 and later: runtime and task status,
 the active task list, the approvals waiting on a human decision, and recent
 activity, with throttled notifications for failures and approval requests.
 .
 The extension holds no secret and runs no command. It reads its state from the
 AgentOS session broker over the user session bus, and a broker that is missing
 or failing degrades to a visible message rather than disturbing the Shell.

Package: agentos-meta
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 agentos-core (>= ${source:Version}),
 agentos-runtime-dsh (>= ${source:Version}),
 agentos-desktop (>= ${source:Version}),
 agentos-gnome-extension (>= ${source:Version})
Description: complete AgentOS installation
 A metapackage that installs the whole AgentOS system: the core service, the
 DeepSeek Harness runtime adapter, the desktop application and session broker,
 and the GNOME Shell extension.
 .
 Install this package for a complete system, or install the individual packages
 to keep a deployment smaller.
